{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1062823763#0_2366900315","relevance":2,"reason":"The result provides some direct evidence about civil engineering work, specializations, collaboration with environmental engineers, and salary, but the document is primarily a list of colleges and universities rather than a dedicated career-description page.","learned":"Civil engineers can work on skyscrapers, bridges, highways, airports, and water resource systems, with specializations such as construction, geotechnical, structural, and transportation engineering."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1341","reason":"The current query has produced dedicated what-does-a-civil-engineer-do pages, so continue to find more grade-3 career-description evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1341"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1942862722#1_2907770649","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1341","rank":6,"snippet":"to designing structures, you may also oversee construction projects. Civil engineers work closely with other construction professionals, such as architects and contractors, to ensure the project is progressing properly. You might survey the site, test ground conditions, and make certain construction materials are maintained. Civil engineers also come up with solutions for weather and geological dilemmas. After construction is complete, you might be responsible for inspecting, repairing, and maintaining structures. Important Facts About This Occupation Entry-level Education Bachelor's degree in civil engineering Licensure Must gain work experience and pass Fundamentals of Engineering exam, as well as other exams, to become licensed<cover>Work Environment Office settings and constructions sites Similar Occupations Architects, civil engineering technicians, construction managers, environmental engineers, landscape architects, mechanical engineers, surveyors, urban and regional planners Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics Specializations Civil engineers may choose to specialize in one aspect of the field, such as materials, coastal, transportation, or environmental engineering.\" , \"start_char\": 422.000000 , \"title\": \"What Does a Civil Engineer Do?</cover>\" , \"url\": \"http://learn.org/articles/What_Does_a_Civil_Engineer_Do.html\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1938640513#0_2896097110","rank":4,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_540082117#0_1191235350","rank":5,"relevance":3}]}}
