{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1139394531#5_1627709847","relevance":2,"reason":"The result gives useful direct evidence about civil engineering career paths and how they differ from construction management, including roles such as environmental engineer, structural engineer, city manager, city planner, and construction planner, but the document is a comparison rather than dedicated to what a civil engineering career is like.","learned":"Civil engineering training can lead to varied paths such as environmental engineering, structural engineering, city management, city planning, and construction planning, while construction engineering tends to lead more directly into construction management roles."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"types of civil engineers\" (+ career careers specialization specializations) (+ structural geotechnical transportation environmental construction))","reason":"Search for pages dedicated to types/specializations of civil engineers, which should directly support the range of careers civil engineering can involve."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"types of civil engineers\" (+ career careers specialization specializations) (+ structural geotechnical transportation environmental construction))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_58002628#0_95342897","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1343","rank":1,"snippet":": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_58002628#0_95342897\" , \"end_char\": 1917.000000 , \"headings\": \"Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering Tweet Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering \" , \"segment\": \"Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering Master Degree Online Home | Resources | Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering Tweet Average Salary Masters in Civil Engineering There are many <cover>types of civil engineers today, like most professions there has been specialization as technology has increasingly grown more complex. Among the disciplines in this category are structural </cover>engineering, transportation, urban engineering and environmental engineering, a relatively recent development in the field. Civil engineers working in the environmental field may find themselves involved in air quality or water quality projects, in other large public works endeavors such as sewer systems, or in the sustainability elements of a construction project or new building. The U.S. Bureau of Labor statistics provides some basic figures for salary averages in the field. According to their survey the median salary for a civil engineer as of Read More [+] Average "}}
