{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_58002628#0_95342897","relevance":2,"reason":"The result provides some direct evidence about civil engineering specializations such as structural, transportation, urban, and environmental engineering, but the document is primarily about average salary for a master's in civil engineering rather than a dedicated explanation of what a civil engineering career is like.","learned":"Civil engineering has multiple specializations, including structural, transportation, urban, and environmental engineering; environmental civil engineers may work on air or water quality, sewer systems, sustainability, and other public works projects."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"civil engineering\" (+ \"why choose\" \"career in civil engineering\" \"civil engineering career\" \"what to expect\") (+ infrastructure communities projects))","reason":"Search for pages explicitly discussing why to choose or what to expect from a civil engineering career, likely to provide dedicated evidence about what the career can be like and its impact on communities and infrastructure."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"civil engineering\" (+ \"why choose\" \"career in civil engineering\" \"civil engineering career\" \"what to expect\") (+ infrastructure communities projects))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1263459082#1_2574612751","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1344","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1263459082#1_2574612751\" , \"end_char\": 2219.000000 , \"headings\": \"Civil Engineering Career Goals Civil Engineering Career Goals Education Requirements Engineering Licensure Planning and Advancement Salary and Growth Trend References \" , \"segment\": \"Obtaining a bachelor’s degree from an accredited educational program is required to be licensed as a professional engineer. Accredited educational programs typically include work experience as an intern to prepare you for a <cover>civil engineering career. Engineering Licensure Civil engineers often work on infrastructure </cover>projects that provide services to the public, which requires a professional engineer license in most states. Two exams are required to obtain a license. The aim of an aspiring civil engineer is to sit for and pass the Fundamentals of Engineering exam administered by the National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying during your senior year of undergraduate studies. This is the first step to obtaining a professional engineer license and shows employers your interest in being a civil engineering career. An entry-level civil engineer objective on a resume should be to finish all licensing "}}
