{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1497447835#2_3225823815","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a dedicated civil engineer job-description page, directly listing typical tasks, duties, responsibilities, specializations, use of design software, specifications, site visits, contractor coordination, bidding documents, and technical reviews.","learned":"Civil engineers may use design software for hydraulic, transportation, and structural systems; specialize in construction, geotechnical, structural, or transportation engineering; prepare design specifications; visit project sites; coordinate with contractors and stakeholders; and prepare bid documents."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1345","reason":"The job-description query is producing directly relevant grade-3 evidence about day-to-day duties, responsibilities, specializations, and work processes, so continue within the remaining budget."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1345"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1505639700#9_3248054816","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1345","rank":3,"snippet":"also start to specialize more and develop expertise in a certain field, which can be both more remunerative and more rewarding. At this time, the median annual salary of a civil engineer is of $63,830. Two emerging fields of importance for civil engineers are the growth in renewable energy projects and the increased importance of maintenance on aging bridges, highways, and other infrastructure. Conclusion Civil engineering is a career with good job prospects and high salaries, but there are plenty of barriers you can encounter in the form of tough college programs. The <cover>civil engineer job description includes planning, managing, and maintaining a construction project, which entails many different duties. </cover>The Professional Engineer license and opportunities to specialize are the main ways to advance as a civil engineer after the first four or five years of working. Master’s degrees are also starting to grow in importance and help engineers learn new and more advanced topics.\" , \"start_char\": 5013.000000 , \"title\": \"Civil Engineer Job Description, Qualifications, and Outlook | Job Descriptions WIKI\" , \"url\": \"https://jobdescriptionswiki.com/civil-engineer-job-description/\" }"}}
